<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="FreddyFreeloader-Bb-Theme" spTempo="142">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1959
Composer:	Miles Davis
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	12-bar blues
Style:	Modal jazz, blues
Key:	B-flat

“Freddie Freeloader” was written by Miles Davis and
recorded for Kind of Blue, released in 1959. Its title’s
origin has competing accounts, including a Philadelphia
bartender and a man who allegedly attended
performances without paying; this uncertainty concerns
the title, not the official authorship credit.</spComments>
